      "notes": "Mille Lacs County, Minnesota (county seat Milaca) publishes its parcels on its own ArcGIS Server 11.3 as MilleLacs_Public_101/MapServer layer 35 (Parcels), 20,083 rows with a taxpayer name on 2026-10-03. THE OWNER IS IN TAXPAYER_NAME, stored LAST/FIRST with a slash. A column called OWNER_NAME exists but is an empty string on about 97 percent of rows (544 of 20,083 populated on 2026-10-03; not NULL, so IS NOT NULL passes while the value is blank), and where it is populated it names a different party from TAXPAYER_NAME (a contract-for-deed holder or an LLC, for example), so the taxpayer is not always the owner of record. UPPER(OWNER_NAME) LIKE 'SMITH%' returns 0 features. OWNER_NAME is deliberately NOT listed as a search field here: the enrichment classifier takes the first owner-looking field, so listing it would route owner lookups to a mostly blank column. The mailing address is TAXPAYER_ADDRESS_1 to _4 (use _1 for the street); the matching OWNER_ADDRESS_1 to _4 columns were not checked. The site address is PROPERTY_ADDRESS with PROPERTY_ZIP and CITY_TWP_NAME. Search with UPPER(TAXPAYER_NAME) LIKE '%SMITH%'. maxRecordCount is 2000. CORS reflects the request Origin (Access-Control-Allow-Origin echoed back, credentials true), and named outFields work. No license text was found. Do not use the statewide Minnesota parcel layers for owner search: the DNR plan_parcels_minnesota layer has owner_name but no county, parcel id or address field, so a query bleeds into neighbouring counties, and the MnGeo plan_parcels_open layer filters by co_code 27095 (20,928 rows) but its owner_name is blank for all but 550 rows (control: Itasca 27061, 0 populated). The same county server also lists Assessors/TaxParcels/MapServer/0, which has only a parcel name and geometry. Verified live 2026-10-03: taxpayer SMITH returned rows (first row parcel 11-010-0100, Milaca Township)."
